                <pb facs="0422" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-15T14:00:00+08:00">August 15, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 15—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>439. Nanking visited by planes about 2 p.m. which dropped a number of bombs
                    apparently on objectives south of city of Nanking, presumably air field.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
